[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n1_godric"
text = "# DRAFT
# Abbot Godric in the chapter house at dusk (night 1), a blanket over his knees. Frail, kind, fatherly.
# He welcomes the porter, blesses him, and speaks of the saint who keeps the house. He dreams badly (the drug; he doesn't know it).
== start
(The abbot sits on the stone bench of the chapter house with a blanket over his knees. He holds out a thin hand.)
Godric: Brother Alric. Come where I can see you. My eyes are better than Anselm's, but not by much in this light.
Godric: Welcome to our house. You're young. Good. The young sleep less and see more.
-> topics

== again
Godric: Still with an old man? The bell will ring for supper soon.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n1_godric_blessing] Will you bless me, Father Abbot? -> blessing
* [if not n1_godric_saint] Tell me about the saint, Father Abbot. -> saint
* [if not n1_godric_porter] What would you have of your porter, Father Abbot? -> porter

== blessing [set n1_godric_blessing] [trust godric 5]
(He lays his hand on your head. It's light and cold, and it shakes.)
Godric: The Lord keep your going out and your coming in. That's the porter's psalm. I chose it for you.
-> topics

== saint [set n1_godric_saint]
Godric: Our saint has kept this house since before London had a mayor. While the relic is on the altar, nothing evil comes in.
Godric: The pilgrims come to the bone, and the bone keeps us. That's how it has always been.
Godric: Lately I dream of the saint. (He looks toward the church, and doesn't finish.) Old men dream.
-> topics

== porter [set n1_godric_porter]
Godric: Keep the gate. Ring the bell. Count us in at Matins, every one.
Godric: And be kind at the grille. Half of London comes to a gate in the dark, and most of it is only cold.
-> topics

== leave
Godric: God keep your going out, brother, and your coming in.
"
